Win12 readable glass (spec section 12.2): the blur effect's on-screen pass already multiplies the blurred
background by a colour matrix (saturation only upstream). This patch builds a second matrix that keeps
Win12Contrast % of the background's contrast and pulls it toward Win12Target % luminance, and uses it for
docks (layer-shell scope dock / NET::Dock) and every plasmashell window (panels, popups, the Win12 menu), so a
translucent bar looks about the same over a white page and a black wallpaper. App windows keep the stock matrix.
Keys: kwinrc [Effect-blur] Win12Contrast (default 100 = off) and Win12Target (default 50); absent keys give
upstream's output. No shader change. colorTransformMatrix moves to colormatrix.h (target .5 = upstream) so the
QTest win12-blur-colormatrix checks the maths without libkwin.

